    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d469">

                <pb facs="0357" n="353" xml:id="pg353"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.941/13197: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-13T19:00:00-04:00">June 13, 1938—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>176. Your 286, June 12, 1 p.m.,<anchor n="59" xml:id="d469-f1"/> and previous
                    telegrams in regard to Japanese notice of the imminent extension of hostilities
                    into the river area between Wuhu and Hukow. Please warn Americans residing in
                    that area and, if you consider it advisable, in the Kiukiang–Nanchang area, of
                    the danger and repeat to them advice that they withdraw by the most practicable
                    routes to places of safety.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
